Package: bigIRT
Title: Item Response Theory for Large Sparse Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Charles",
           family = "Driver",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "charles.driver@psychologie.uzh.ch",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4174-2970"))
Description: Fits binary item response theory (IRT) models for large and sparse
    data in long format, by marginal maximum likelihood with a Laplace
    approximation to the integral over person abilities, or by the joint
    posterior mode over items and persons. Supports 1PL to 4PL models,
    multidimensional and confirmatory loading structures with an estimated
    latent correlation, covariate effects on ability and on each item
    parameter, empirical-Bayes prior adaptation, and post-estimation tools for
    information, reliability, item fit, held-out prediction and simulation.
